    FEAT-0002: recognize customers with four interests as Community Enthusiasts

    Marketing wants a tier between Frequent Customer (3 categories) and
    Community Champion (5): a customer who has tried four of the five
    categories should be recognized before they round out the set.

    REFACTOR-0002 already gathered every rule relating interests to status
    into Customer.status, so the new tier is one more threshold there —
    register(), the waitlist path, and the catalogue seeding loop don't
    change at all.

    Adds Test 42f to lock in the new tier: a customer with four interests
    (c03) now reads as a Community Enthusiast. Test 42b is untouched — it
    already exercises a three-interest customer (c04), which still reads
    as Frequent Customer under the new thresholds.

diff --git a/src/Customer.ts b/src/Customer.ts
index ad7ccae..c41f5b2 100644
--- a/src/Customer.ts
+++ b/src/Customer.ts
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ export class Customer {

 	public get status(): string {
 		if (this.interests.length >= 5) return "Community Champion";
+		if (this.interests.length >= 4) return "Community Enthusiast";
 		if (this.interests.length >= 3) return "Frequent Customer";
 		return "Default";
 	}
diff --git a/test/parkboard.spec.ts b/test/parkboard.spec.ts
